# Gravity, from culture/essays/knowing.md. Heaven full of people is earth: every way out falls back to others.
# Each escape route is computed from the one before it, and each must equal OR(people, ground).
let gravity = load gravity.bench
show gravity
claim correct(gravity)            # every escape route is bound: it returns to people or ground, on all 4 inputs
claim nots(gravity) = 0           # no negation anywhere: every route is built from OR alone (it can only add, never cancel)
claim gates(gravity) = base(gravity)   # no wasted gate: 4 gates are the least this function needs without a NOT
# In tandem, the physics. The circuit above is the essay's argument shape. This check is the physical fact it echoes:
# on exact rational orbit states, a body is bound (a closed orbit, e < 1) exactly when its energy E < 0 (physics/cosmos).
# The same script also holds the age of the universe, which is a numerical test, not an exact one.
check "python3 -I physics/cosmos/check.py"
record culture/essays essays checked-finite "gravity.ath: every escape route in culture/essays/knowing.md (heaven, leaving town, the party, the mirror) computes OR(people, ground) on all 4 inputs. The argument's shape, not the essay's truth."
